<title>UK: UK Connex train drivers vote to ban overtime.</title>
<headline>UK Connex train drivers vote to ban overtime.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Train drivers for south east England regional operator Connex, part of Cie Generale des Eaux, have voted to ban overtime, the Press Association news agency quoted their union ASLEF as saying on Thursday.</p>
<p>The move threatened to affect services on busy routes into London from Kent.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom 44 171 542 7947</p>
</text>
